From b467b2d602b5accb6144010b925fde051bdf9df2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Norton <greg@serenityos.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:46:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] LibDebug: Drive DebugSession through host ptrace on Linux

Map Serenity's PT_* requests to the PTRACE_* equivalents, copy registers
field-by-field from glibc's user_regs_struct (the layouts differ), parse
loaded libraries from /proc/<pid>/maps instead of Serenity's vm API, and
skip the PT_ATTACH round trip when the debuggee was already started with
TRACEME. Watchpoints need x86 debug-register ptrace support that host
kernels do not expose through this ABI, so they stay Serenity-only.

glibc's waitpid does not accept the BSD-style WEXITED flag, so use plain
waitpid on host builds (it reports exits too). Also guard Debugger against
a null library_at(ip): host debuggees stop inside stripped libraries or
anonymous memory where Serenity's loader breakpoint never lands.
